[ROOT CAUSE GROUP 11] GATE / MEMBERSHIP CACHE RACES
  MODULE 12 _GATE_CACHE and _CHATMEM_CACHE are global dicts with TTL; concurrent gate_check calls can race on write.
  Cache stores status string; after kick the cache still returns “member” until TTL expires, allowing expired users to keep interacting.
  setgate1 clears only part of the cache; other processes keep the old id.
  check_gate returns False on any exception, treating network blips as “left channel”.

[ROOT CAUSE GROUP 12] REFERRAL & INVITE LINK LIFECYCLE BUGS
  MODULE 16 gen_link creates Telegram invite with expire_date but also stores a separate Settings key with its own expiry; the two can drift.
  credit_referral and on_join_complete both attempt to set referred_by and credit tokens; double-credit possible under concurrent join events.
  ref_maintenance_loop deletes expired Settings but never cancels the corresponding Telegram invite link.
  MODULE 15 handle_join_request approves referral channel unconditionally; no check that the join came from a valid ref link.
  Daily cap and lifetime counters are updated without a single atomic transaction covering both the new user and the owner in all paths.

[ROOT CAUSE GROUP 13] BOOT / RECOVERY / SCHEDULER ORDERING
  MODULE 22 sets SYSTEM_LOCKED=True, runs recover_and_finalize_boot, then sets False; any handler that fires during the window sees locked state, but webhook server is started after unlock.
  recover_and_finalize_boot never schedules the periodic jobs (check_expiry, check_overstay, check_inactivity, reset_referrals, ref_maintenance_loop); they are defined but never added to the scheduler.
  EXPIRING_SOON_SET is populated at boot then only mutated by add_expiring_user; if a package is activated while the set is being iterated in check_expiry, RuntimeError or missed expiry occurs.
  BOOT_LOCK_KEY Redis key is set with RECOVERY_MAX_RUNTIME_SEC but the recovery itself has no overall timeout; a hung Alby call can leave the key stuck until TTL.

[ROOT CAUSE GROUP 14] HTTP SESSION / RESOURCE LEAK & TIMEOUT MISUSE
  MODULE 02 get_http creates a single global ClientSession with WEBHOOK_TIMEOUT; all Alby and self-ping calls share it.
  close_http is only called on process exit; under long-running process the connector limit can be exhausted.
  MODULE 17A/17B alby_semaphore is created twice (once per module) with the same ALBY_RPS value; two independent semaphores double the allowed concurrency.
  aiohttp timeout is set only on ClientSession construction; individual requests that pass a different timeout are ignored or raise.
  MODULE 10/22 ping_self swallows all exceptions; health endpoint can be down indefinitely with no alert.

